# Shared project instructions

Read `knowledge/INDEX.md`, `knowledge/project.md`, `knowledge/integration.md`, and `communication/PROTOCOL.md` before acting. Read `knowledge/handoff.md` unless the integration contract assigns blind Verification. The role assigned by the current `mission-control/start-*.md` contract determines responsibility; this file grants no role by itself.

Inspect actual artifacts before reporting results. Keep epistemic, operational, authority, and verification state distinct. Current human user decisions and governance govern authority; direct sources and maintained project knowledge govern epistemic claims; inspected artifacts and running systems govern operational claims; complete findings and cited evidence govern verification claims. Perform clear, reversible, authorized local actions autonomously. Return objectives, consequential subject-matter positions, rights, attribution, publication, external effects, and difficult-to-reverse consequences to the human user.

Use maintained project knowledge as the persistent working context. An external Vault is an optional long-term source and remains inactive unless `knowledge/integration.md` configures it. Research is the single writer for `knowledge/` unless `knowledge/integration.md` names a narrower owner. Operations returns candidate consequences through its immutable outbox. Verification reports its complete finding first and only to the human user and never produces a correction; Research receives a finding only after human-authorized routing. Research verifies accepted findings, integrates them into the responsible Knowledge Document, and records the transition in `knowledge/journal.md`. Keep `knowledge/handoff.md` for open received deltas only and remove each point after integration or rejection.

Communicate outcome first. A source link that the human user must inspect requires a one-to-three-sentence substantive synthesis, its practical significance, and the concrete point to assess. Report raw test counts only when they establish a relevant claim.
